      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60285ca04963ba22994f485b|full_name}: The audio overrides are good and decent for some situations and may address the example given here since it's kind of vague about how it wants the audio to be treated specifically, but the voice settings are not quite what this canny is requesting with its proposed implementation.\nThis canny is requesting the ability for players to copy their or other player's voices to other audio sources. The voice settings are good for players to have a \"voice of god\" if they want to communicate something to everyone in the world. But they're not really a good replacement for having something like a walkie talkie, intercom, or stage speakers in the world since they can't spatialize or attenuate in any remotely controllable fashion.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
